"><span class=\"fn\">α</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`iterRange f lo hi x` applies `f lo`, `f (lo + 1)`, …, `f (hi - 1)` to `x`, in this order: the\nmodel of a loop from `lo` up to `hi - 1` whose step `j` maps its state by `f j`. It is `x` when\n`hi ≤ lo`.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Stride.html#ScalarArray.iterRange","kind":"def","line":38,"name":"ScalarArray.iterRange","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/7ffd513add11df79848981c4efa28480b0e2e483/ScalarArray/Stride.lean#L38-L45"}}],"imports":["Init","ScalarArray.Internal"],"instances":[{"className":"Decidable","name":"ScalarArray.instDecidableEqStride","typeNames":["Eq"]},{"className":"Repr","name":"ScalarArray.instReprStride","typeNames":["ScalarArray.Stride"]},{"className":"Decidable","name":"ScalarArray.Stride.instDecidableFits","typeNames":["ScalarArray.Stride.Fits"]}],"name":"ScalarArray.Stride"}